# PHASE 3 – AGGREGATION AND GROUPING

# 17. Aggregate Functions

Aggregate functions calculate results from multiple rows.

## COUNT()

Counts records.

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM employees;
```

## SUM()

Calculates total.

```sql
SELECT SUM(salary)
FROM employees;
```

## AVG()

Calculates average.

```sql
SELECT AVG(salary)
FROM employees;
```

## MAX()

Finds maximum value.

```sql
SELECT MAX(salary)
FROM employees;
```

## MIN()

Finds minimum value.

```sql
SELECT MIN(salary)
FROM employees;
```

### Important COUNT Difference

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM employees;
```

Counts rows.

```sql
SELECT COUNT(dept_id)
FROM employees;
```

Counts non-NULL values in `dept_id`.

```sql
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT dept_id)
FROM employees;
```

Counts distinct non-NULL department IDs.

