# 22. CASE Statement

CASE applies conditional logic inside SQL queries.

```sql
SELECT
    name,
    salary,
    CASE
        WHEN salary >= 25000 THEN 'High'
        WHEN salary >= 18000 THEN 'Medium'
        ELSE 'Low'
    END AS salary_category
FROM employees;
```

CASE can be used in:

- SELECT
- ORDER BY
- GROUP BY expressions
- UPDATE
- Aggregations

Example:

```sql
SELECT
    SUM(
        CASE
            WHEN department = 'IT' THEN 1
            ELSE 0
        END
    ) AS it_employees
FROM employees;
```

