# 23. NULL Handling

NULL represents missing or unknown data.

Important: NULL is not equal to zero or an empty string.

## IS NULL

```sql
SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE dept_id IS NULL;
```

## IS NOT NULL

```sql
SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE dept_id IS NOT NULL;
```

## COALESCE

Returns the first non-NULL value.

```sql
SELECT
    name,
    COALESCE(dept_id, 0) AS department_id
FROM employees;
```

## NULLIF

Returns NULL if two expressions are equal.

```sql
SELECT NULLIF(10, 10);
```

## IFNULL

MySQL-specific function.

```sql
SELECT IFNULL(dept_id, 0)
FROM employees;
```

SQL Server provides `ISNULL`; PostgreSQL and standard SQL support `COALESCE`.

