# 27. Set Operators

Set operators combine results from multiple SELECT statements.

## UNION

Combines results and removes duplicates.

```sql
SELECT name FROM employees
UNION
SELECT name FROM customers;
```

## UNION ALL

Combines results and retains duplicates.

```sql
SELECT name FROM employees
UNION ALL
SELECT name FROM customers;
```

## INTERSECT

Returns common rows.

```sql
SELECT name FROM employees
INTERSECT
SELECT name FROM customers;
```

## EXCEPT

Returns rows from the first query that do not appear in the second.

```sql
SELECT name FROM employees
EXCEPT
SELECT name FROM customers;
```

Support for INTERSECT and EXCEPT depends on the database version. Oracle commonly uses MINUS for the equivalent of EXCEPT.

Important: Both queries must return the same number of compatible columns.

