# 29. Views

A view is a saved SQL query that behaves like a virtual table.

```sql
CREATE VIEW high_salary_employees AS
SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE salary > 20000;
```

Use the view:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM high_salary_employees;
```

Delete a view:

```sql
DROP VIEW high_salary_employees;
```

## Materialized View

A materialized view stores query results physically and generally needs refreshing.

Support and refresh syntax vary by database.

### View vs Materialized View

| View | Materialized View |
|---|---|
| Stores query definition | Stores query result |
| Usually calculates when queried | Reads stored result |
| Reflects underlying data according to query behavior | Can become stale until refreshed |
| Uses no separate result storage in a normal view | Requires storage |

