# 30. Indexes

An index helps the database locate records more efficiently.

Example:

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_employee_salary
ON employees(salary);
```

Composite index:

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_department_salary
ON employees(dept_id, salary);
```

Delete index syntax varies by database.

PostgreSQL:

```sql
DROP INDEX idx_employee_salary;
```

## Types of Indexes

Common concepts:

- B-tree index
- Hash index
- Unique index
- Composite index
- Clustered index
- Non-clustered index
- Partial or filtered index

Availability and behavior differ across database systems.

## Advantages

- Can speed up filtering.
- Can improve join performance.
- Can help sorting and lookup operations.

## Disadvantages

- Requires storage.
- Can slow INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE.
- Needs maintenance.
- Too many indexes can reduce performance.

