# 31. Primary Key and Foreign Key

## Primary Key

Uniquely identifies a row.

```sql
CREATE TABLE departments (
    dept_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    dept_name VARCHAR(100)
);
```

## Foreign Key

References a key in another table.

```sql
CREATE TABLE employees (
    emp_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100),
    dept_id INT,
    FOREIGN KEY (dept_id)
        REFERENCES departments(dept_id)
);
```

Relationship:

```text
Departments
------------
dept_id (PK)
dept_name
     |
     | 1-to-many
     |
Employees
---------
emp_id (PK)
name
dept_id (FK)
```

## Types of Relationships

1. One-to-One
2. One-to-Many
3. Many-to-Many

A many-to-many relationship is commonly implemented using a junction table.

