# 32. Normalization

Normalization organizes relational tables to reduce unnecessary duplication and improve data integrity.

## First Normal Form (1NF)

- Each column contains atomic values.
- Avoid repeating groups.

## Second Normal Form (2NF)

- Must satisfy 1NF.
- Non-key attributes must depend on the whole candidate key, not just part of a composite candidate key.

## Third Normal Form (3NF)

- Must satisfy 2NF.
- Non-key attributes should not depend transitively on candidate keys.

## Example

Instead of storing department name repeatedly in employee records, store departments separately and reference them using `dept_id`.

### Why normalization?

- Reduces duplication.
- Improves data integrity.
- Simplifies updates.

Data warehouses may also use denormalized models such as star schemas for analytical performance.

