# 38. SQL Functions and Triggers

## User-Defined Function

A function returns a value or table, depending on the database.

PostgreSQL example:

```sql
CREATE FUNCTION add_numbers(a INT, b INT)
RETURNS INT
LANGUAGE SQL
AS $$
    SELECT a + b;
$$;
```

Execute:

```sql
SELECT add_numbers(10, 20);
```

## Trigger

A trigger automatically executes in response to specified database events.

Common events:

