# 42. Incremental Data Loading

Incremental loading processes only new or changed records rather than reloading the entire dataset.

Example: Extract records updated after the last successful load.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM source_orders
WHERE updated_at > TIMESTAMP '2026-11-17 00:00:00';
```

A real pipeline should store and retrieve its last successful watermark rather than hardcode the timestamp.

## Full Load vs Incremental Load

| Full Load | Incremental Load |
|---|---|
| Loads all records | Loads new or changed records |
| Can be expensive for large datasets | Often more efficient |
| Simple to implement | Requires watermark or change tracking |
| Useful for initial loads | Useful for regular updates |

## Important Concepts

- Watermark
- Last processed timestamp
- Change Data Capture (CDC)
- Upsert
- Deduplication
- Idempotency

