# 43. UPSERT

UPSERT means inserting a record if it does not exist, or updating it if it already exists.

PostgreSQL example:

```sql
INSERT INTO customers (
    customer_id,
    name,
    city
)
VALUES (
    101,
    'Ankit',
    'Bengaluru'
)
ON CONFLICT (customer_id)
DO UPDATE SET
    name = EXCLUDED.name,
    city = EXCLUDED.city;
```

UPSERT is useful for incremental data pipelines and synchronizing records.

Syntax varies across databases. SQL Server, MySQL and Oracle have their own approaches.

