# 44. Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD)

SCD is a data warehousing technique used to manage changes in dimension data over time.

## SCD Type 0

Keep the original value unchanged.

## SCD Type 1

Overwrite the old value.

Example: Update the customer's city without maintaining history.

## SCD Type 2

Preserve historical records by creating a new version.

Typical columns:

- customer_id
- city
- effective_start_date
- effective_end_date
- is_current

Example:

| customer_id | city | start_date | end_date | is_current |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 101 | Nagpur | 2025-01-01 | 2026-01-01 | False |
| 101 | Bengaluru | 2026-01-01 | NULL | True |

SCD Type 2 is useful when historical changes must be retained.

